\end{equation}
Now, substituting the generalized purities of $\sigma$ at high temperature, we get
\begin{equation}
    |R| = \bigO{\frac{1}{D} \exp(\bigO{N \beta^2})}.
\end{equation}
This means that for a sufficiently high constant temperature, $|R|$ is exponentially small in $N$, and we establish
\begin{equation}
